        "Name": "Chronic Brain Lesion MRI with Manual Lesion Segmentations (CCNRP, Cambridge)",
        "ReferencesAndLinks": null
      },
      "readme": "This dataset contains defaced structural MRI scans and corresponding lesion masks from individuals with chronic focal brain lesions (CCNRP cohort).\n\nModalities:\n- T1-weighted MRI\n\nLesion masks:\n- Binary lesion masks are provided for each participant\n- Masks are in the same native space as the corresponding T1-weighted image\n- Lesions are chronic and non-progressive at the time of scanning?\n- Lesions arise from heterogeneous aetiologies, including ischemic stroke and surgical resections (exact distribution not provided at the individual level)\n- Lesions were manually delineated on a case-by-case basis by a senior neurologist using the MRIcron software.\n\nImage orientation and preprocessing:\n- Detailed preprocessing histories (e.g., software versions, normalization steps) are not consistently available across participants due to the archival nature of the dataset and are therefore not included\n\nDe-identification:\n- All anatomical images have been defaced prior to upload\n- No personal identifiers are included in filenames or metadata\n- Clinical dates and detailed medical histories are not included due to heterogeneity and privacy considerations\n\nParticipants:\n- The dataset includes 204 participants in total\n- Participant-level demographic or clinical variables (e.g., age, sex, aetiology) are not provided in the public release\n\nIntended use:\n- Evaluation and development of automated lesion segmentation methods\n- Methodological research in lesion–symptom mapping\n\n",
